```css
:root {
  --ocean-surface: #00485E;
}
```

This variable can be used to style ocean-related elements, such as waves or backgrounds, in your UI design. You can then reference it in your CSS like so:

```css
.wave {
  background-color: var(--ocean-surface);
}
```

The `#00485E` value represents a deep blue color, reminiscent of the ocean's depths.

